---
// two-component-receptor — the central idea of the MC2R page. On its own,
// MC2R is stranded in the endoplasmic reticulum. Its accessory protein MRAP1
// escorts it to the cell surface and reshapes it so it can read ACTH — the
// one melanocortin that carries both the shared His-Phe-Arg-Trp "message"
// and the basic Lys-Lys-Arg-Arg-Pro "address" MC2R demands. The MSH peptides
// carry only the message, so they cannot switch it on. Schematic; SVG-only,
// wrap in <Figure>.
---

<svg
  class="tcr-fig"
  viewBox="0 0 640 330"
  role="img"
  aria-labelledby="tcr-t tcr-d"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <title id="tcr-t">A two-component receptor: why MC2R needs MRAP1 and answers only to ACTH</title>
  <desc id="tcr-d"
    >Left: inside the cell, MC2R alone is stranded in the endoplasmic reticulum
    and never reaches the surface. Middle: MRAP1, a small single-pass protein
    that forms an antiparallel dimer, binds MC2R and escorts it to the plasma
    membrane. Right: at the surface the MC2R–MRAP1 complex reads ACTH, which
    carries the shared His-Phe-Arg-Trp message plus a basic Lys-Lys-Arg-Arg-Pro
    address. Alpha-, beta- and gamma-MSH carry the message but not the address,
    so they cannot activate MC2R.</desc
  >

  <!-- stage 1: stranded in the ER -->
  <rect class="card" x="20" y="22" width="180" height="118" rx="12" />
  <text x="110" y="46" text-anchor="middle" class="head">Alone</text>
  <text x="110" y="64" text-anchor="middle" class="sub">endoplasmic reticulum</text>
  <rect class="rec-box dim" x="70" y="76" width="80" height="34" rx="8" />
  <text x="110" y="98" text-anchor="middle" class="rec dim-t">MC2R</text>
  <text x="110" y="130" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">stranded inside the cell</text>

  <!-- stage 2: MRAP1 joins -->
  <rect class="card hot" x="230" y="22" width="180" height="118" rx="12" />
  <text x="320" y="46" text-anchor="middle" class="head hot-t">With MRAP1</text>
  <text x="320" y="64" text-anchor="middle" class="sub">escorted to the cell surface</text>
  <rect class="rec-box hot" x="262" y="76" width="80" height="34" rx="8" />
  <text x="302" y="98" text-anchor="middle" class="rec hot-t">MC2R</text>
  <!-- antiparallel MRAP1 dimer: two strands, opposite arrowheads -->
  <path class="mrap" d="M350 80 L378 80" />
  <polygon class="mrap-arrow" points="378,76 386,80 378,84" />
  <path class="mrap" d="M386 102 L358 102" />
  <polygon class="mrap-arrow" points="358,98 350,102 358,106" />
  <text x="368" y="94" text-anchor="middle" class="mini">MRAP1</text>
  <text x="320" y="130" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">an antiparallel dimer escorts it</text>

  <!-- stage 3: at the surface reading ACTH -->
  <rect class="card hot" x="440" y="22" width="180" height="118" rx="12" />
  <text x="530" y="46" text-anchor="middle" class="head hot-t">At the surface</text>
  <text x="530" y="64" text-anchor="middle" class="sub">reads ACTH → Gs → cAMP</text>
  <rect class="rec-box hot" x="472" y="76" width="80" height="34" rx="8" />
  <text x="512" y="98" text-anchor="middle" class="rec hot-t">MC2R</text>
  <path class="mrap" d="M560 80 L588 80" />
  <polygon class="mrap-arrow" points="588,76 596,80 588,84" />
  <path class="mrap" d="M596 102 L568 102" />
  <polygon class="mrap-arrow" points="568,98 560,102 568,106" />
  <text x="578" y="94" text-anchor="middle" class="mini">MRAP1</text>
  <text x="530" y="130" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">cortisol is made</text>

  <!-- arrows between stages -->
  <path class="branch hot" d="M200 81 L230 81" />
  <polygon class="arrow" points="222,76 230,81 222,86" />
  <path class="branch hot" d="M410 81 L440 81" />
  <polygon class="arrow" points="432,76 440,81 432,86" />

  <!-- travelling emphasis dot along the escort path -->
  <circle class="pulse" r="4">
    <animateMotion dur="3.6s" repeatCount="indefinite" keyPoints="0;1" keyTimes="0;1"
      path="M200 81 L440 81" />
  </circle>

  <!-- ligand panel: message + address -->
  <text x="20" y="178" class="head">What the complex demands of its ligand</text>

  <!-- ACTH row -->
  <text x="20" y="208" class="lig">ACTH</text>
  <rect class="seg msg" x="118" y="194" width="150" height="22" rx="6" />
  <text x="193" y="209" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">His-Phe-Arg-Trp · message</text>
  <rect class="seg addr" x="276" y="194" width="170" height="22" rx="6" />
  <text x="361" y="209" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">Lys-Lys-Arg-Arg-Pro · address</text>
  <path class="branch hot" d="M446 205 L490 205" />
  <polygon class="arrow" points="482,200 490,205 482,210" />
  <text x="498" y="209" class="verdict hot-t">activates MC2R</text>

  <!-- MSH row -->
  <text x="20" y="250" class="lig">α-, β-, γ-MSH</text>
  <rect class="seg msg" x="118" y="236" width="150" height="22" rx="6" />
  <text x="193" y="251" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">His-Phe-Arg-Trp · message</text>
  <rect class="seg empty" x="276" y="236" width="170" height="22" rx="6" />
  <text x="361" y="251" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t dim-t">no address</text>
  <path class="branch" d="M446 247 L490 247" />
  <polygon class="arrow dimfill" points="482,242 490,247 482,252" />
  <text x="498" y="251" class="verdict dim-t">silent at MC2R</text>

  <text x="20" y="286" class="line">The message alone is enough for MC1R and MC3R–MC5R. MC2R alone also checks the address —</text>
  <text x="20" y="304" class="line">the built-in guard that keeps pigment and appetite signals from triggering cortisol.</text>
</svg>

